--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -33,3 +33,27 @@ Decisions that later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) rely on:
 - Object members are looked up as own properties only: `/constructor` on `{}` throws, and an own
   `"__proto__"` member (from `JSON.parse`) resolves normally.
 - A token applied to a primitive or `null` throws.
+
+### JSON Patch — RFC 6902 (`src/patch.ts`)
+
+- `applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the operations (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`,
+  `test`) in order and returns the result as a new value, or throws `JsonPatchError` (with `index` and
+  `operation` of the offending operation, `index` undefined if the patch is not an array; a
+  `JsonPointerError` behind it is kept as `cause`).
+- `JsonPatchOperation` is the TypeScript type of one operation.
+
+Decisions:
+
+- Inputs are never mutated: the document is deep-copied once, then patched in place; inserted values
+  (`add`/`replace` values, `copy` sources) are deep-copied too, so the result shares nothing with
+  the inputs. A failing patch therefore has no partial effect.
+- The whole patch is validated (shape, known `op`, string `path`/`from` that parse as pointers,
+  `value` present for `add`/`replace`/`test` — `null` is allowed) before any operation is applied.
+  Unknown members of an operation are ignored (section 4).
+- Paths are resolved like `resolvePointer` (own properties only, strict array indices). `-` is only
+  accepted as the last token of an `add` target (or of a `move`/`copy` `path`).
+- `replace` keeps the position of an object member; `add` on an existing member replaces it in place.
+  `__proto__` members are written with `defineProperty`, so they never change a prototype.
+- `remove` of the whole document (`""`) throws. `move` from a location to itself is a no-op (once
+  `from` is known to exist); `move` into a proper child of `from` throws.
+- `test` uses JSON equality (section 4.6): same type, objects compared regardless of member order.
